  "result_json": "{\"executive_interpretation\":{\"observation_ids\":[\"2026:revenue_profit_growth\"],\"interpretation\":{\"string\":\"Revenue and operating income grew alongside operating cash flow, reflecting higher cash collections from customers and lower income tax payments, while foreign currency movements also contributed positively to reported metrics.\"0},\"supporting_passage_ids\":[\"sec:838fe0caa8c807af7d81b902\",\"sec:2b952351bdb846469a21de3f\"]},\"primary_finding\":{\"interpretation\":{\"string\":\"Operating cash flow rose substantially, yet free cash flow declined because cash purchases of property and equipment increased at an even faster pace. This divergence shows that expanding capital investments absorbed more cash than the higher operating cash generation provided.\"0},\"supporting_passage_ids\":[\"sec:838fe0caa8c807af7d81b902\",\"sec:37f112340286145a10842b03\"],\"alternative_explanation\":{\"string\":\"The reduction in free cash flow could reflect accelerated infrastructure timing or broader multi-year hardware deliveries rather than an ongoing structural deterioration in cash generation.\"0},\"limitations\":{\"string\":\"Cash PP&E purchases represent total company-wide property and equipment outlays and do not isolate AI spending or lease-inclusive commitments.\"0}},\"findings\":[{\"observation_ids\":[\"2026:investment_intensity\"],\"interpretation\":{\"string\":\"Cash investment intensity increased markedly as property and equipment outlays claimed a significantly larger share of revenue and operating cash flow, driven by ongoing infrastructure expansions.\"0},\"supporting_passage_ids\":[\"sec:37f112340286145a10842b03\"],\"alternative_explanation\":{\"string\":\"Higher investment intensity may reflect front-loaded procurement cycles or temporary supply-chain catch-up rather than a permanently elevated capital-intensity baseline.\"0},\"limitations\":{\"string\":\"Capital expenditure ratios do not measure capacity utilisation, eventual monetisation timing, or economic return on invested capital.\"0}},{\"observation_ids\":[\"2026:earnings_conversion_tension\"],\"interpretation\":{\"string\":\"Net income improved substantially, while free-cash-flow conversion deteriorated because cash capital expenditures outpaced the growth in operating cash flow and net earnings.\"0},\"supporting_passage_ids\":[\"sec:838fe0caa8c807af7d81b902\",\"sec:2b952351bdb846469a21de3f\"],\"alternative_explanation\":{\"string\":\"The divergence between net income and free cash flow might be driven by non-operating investment gains and timing differences in working capital rather than weaker underlying cash conversion.\"0},\"limitations\":{\"string\":\"Net income includes non-operating investment gains that do not generate cash flow and should not be equated with underlying operating cash conversion.\"0}}],\"risks\":[{\"interpretation\":{\"string\":\"Electricity generation and transmission infrastructure constraints, along with power connection delays or regulatory requirements, could restrict the ability to develop or expand datacenter capacity.\"0},\"supporting_passage_ids\":[\"sec:56d67b25b672d6b595978ea9\"],\"limitations\":{\"string\":\"Disclosed risks represent potential operational headwinds and management caution; they do not indicate that these conditions have materialised or impaired financial performance.\"0}}],\"unanswered_questions\":[\"What are the expected utilisation rates and monetisation timelines for the newly constructed datacenters and compute capacity?\"0,\"How much of the total property and equipment additions are committed to specific product lines versus general corporate infrastructure?\"0,\"To what extent will future power availability constraints and utility requirements impact the pace of upcoming capital expenditure programs?\"0]}"
